{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"662041d2f570e2fe5a0735418c51fd813c403fd3e7ff095f8baeb8a5dd3a9ebb","digest":{"component_or_area":"plan-review novelty scorer and eval runner dispatch","key_entities":["score_novelty","src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify.py:759","_score_floor_novelty","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py","run_case","src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py:156","REVIEW_RESULT events","coverage.remediation.eligible","coverage.narrowed","drop_reason"],"problem_keywords":["novelty scorer","plan review","floor drops","remediation eligible","eval runner","carryover discrimination"],"propositions":["The plan-review novelty scorer (score_novelty) correctly discriminates carryover findings (92/92 same-norm_id findings score < 0.7) and novel findings (185/449 score >= 0.7), indicating healthy scorer behavior.","Post-2026-07-12 remediation-eligible reviews produce substantive floor drops (33/35 eligible reviews have coverage.narrowed=true with ~111 total floored findings), contradicting the initial zero-drop measurement artifact caused by incomplete REVIEW_RESULT event parsing.","The live eval runner (eval_solver.run_case) cannot dispatch plan-review-novelty prompts, accepting only criterion ids, code-review prompts, and three hardcoded agentic reviewers, requiring direct runtime scorer path invocation to validate the scorer.","BLOCK-loop rounds remain ineligible for floor drops because signed=False, a structural gap independent of scorer health addressed by a separate story ticket."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785817814890628423,"uuid":"3c7bb3af-f1aa-459b-9fbb-d083edfd4503"}